<dataset>
	<!--
		Six users a ban moved into the ban group (8). The test adds the bans
		itself, because phpBB 3.3 and 4.0 keep bans in different tables:

		- user 2: no longer banned, membership created by the ban - should
		  be removed from group 8 and have their default restored to 7.
		- user 3: still banned by username - must be left completely alone.
		- user 4: no longer banned, but already a member of group 8 before
		  the ban (move_new_membership = 0) - keeps that membership; only
		  the default group is restored (to 7) and the tracking row removed.
		- user 5: no longer banned, but also restricted into the same group
		  8 - keeps the membership the restriction still needs; the default
		  group is restored and the ban tracking row removed.
		- user 6: username ban lifted, but their email domain (*@spam.example)
		  is still banned - must be left completely alone.
		- user 7: username ban lifted; their registration IP (198.51.100.7)
		  is still in a banned range, but that is not where they visit from
		  now - restored like user 2.
	-->
